--- !u!114 &1053947339
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 1053947338}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 1782210d8beb0b941b936f373a634e5f, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::TutorialController
  tutorialPopup:
  - pages:
    - title: Spell Creation
      description: The main combat tools at your disposal are Spells. In a real match,
        you will start with some Spells already created and will be able to edit
        them or create new ones, but here you'll learn how to make your own.
      sprite: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 74d038592bf535f4b8727bacafba3513, type: 3}
      videoClip: {fileID: 0}
    - title: Spell Creation
      description: 'First, you''ll click the + Card to create a new Spell. Then,
        you''ll be able to craft the spell by clicking twice on the Spell card, or
        by clicking on the Spell card to select it, and then pressing the Edit Spell
        button. '
      sprite: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 1453bbc79b0dc0b4e9c00f819be3bc97, type: 3}
      videoClip: {fileID: 0}
    - title: Spell Creation
      description: When the Spell Card is selected, you can also click on one of
        the Equipped Spell Slots below to equip the Spell to be able to cast it with
        the corresponding button.
      sprite: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 1fb8770ac83387f4bb58860449e94e14, type: 3}
      videoClip: {fileID: 0}
    - title: Spell Creation
      description: You can delete a selected Spell by clicking on the X button next
        to the Spell Card.
      sprite: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 2b8a03d05fbcd5f41a51dd8f280e9b82, type: 3}
      videoClip: {fileID: 0}
    popupShown: 0
  - pages:
    - title: Spell Crafting - Basics
      description: 'This is where you craft your Spell. From left to right, you have:
        your Rune Inventory, with all your obtained Runes; your Spell Tablet, where
        you connect the Runes to make the Spell; and the Rune Description, where
        you can read the informations of each Rune, and configure some options for
        some Rune types.'
      sprite: {fileID: 0}
      videoClip: {fileID: 0}
    - title: Spell Crafting - Basics
      description: 'You can change the name of your Spell and its Glyph to better
        represent it. '
      sprite: {fileID: 0}
      videoClip: {fileID: 0}
    - title: Spell Crafting - Basics
      description: Runes are the building blocks for your Spell. Different Rune combinations
        will result in different Spell effects. There are multiple types of Runes,
        each serving a different function within the Spell.
      sprite: {fileID: 0}
      videoClip: {fileID: 0}
    - title: Spell Crafting - Basics
      description: 'In addition to their innate effects, each Rune contains its own
        stats, which are added to the Spell''s stats once the Rune is rightfully
        connected. Runes also have Cooldown costs, which may increase or decrease
        the cooldown of the Spell. Each rune also has its own Rarity, which defines
        the quality of its stats.

'
      sprite: {fileID: 21300000, guid: f0a4299763d6a664184eea3cb3ce974c, type: 3}
      videoClip: {fileID: 0}
    - title: Spell Crafting - Core
      description: 'Core Runes are responsible for defining the type of Spell that
        will be cast. They are required for the Spell to work and must be placed
        on the center slot of the Rune Tablet. '
      sprite: {fileID: 0}
      videoClip: {fileID: 0}
    - title: Spell Crafting - Core
      description: "The Core Rune contains the stat multipliers of the Spell. Every
        stat from any rune will be multiplied by these values before it is added
        to the Spell\u2019s stats. The multipliers vary depending on which type of
        Core Rune that Spell is using."
      sprite: {fileID: 0}
      videoClip: {fileID: 0}
    - title: Spell Crafting - Core
      description: "In the Core Rune's description, it\u2019s possible to configure
        what the Spell collides with and what it doesn't."
      sprite: {fileID: 0}
      videoClip: {fileID: 0}
    popupShown: 0
  - pages:
    - title: Spell Crafting - Expanding
      description: 'To add another Rune to a spell, that Rune must be connected via
        one of its Sockets to the Core Rune or to a sequence of Runes connected to
        the Core Rune. To make a connection, the Sockets must have the same shape. '
      sprite: {fileID: 0}
      videoClip: {fileID: 0}
    - title: Spell Crafting - Trajectory
      description: Trajectory Runes are responsible for defining how your Spell will
        move, and usually add speed to it as well.
      sprite: {fileID: 21300000, guid: e1aa291534eb3664b9e6b849c3ad4313, type: 3}
      videoClip: {fileID: 0}
    popupShown: 0
  - pages:
    - title: Spell Crafting - Effect
      description: An Effect Rune is required to determine what the Spell will do
        when it hits a Creature. It can either deal Damage or Heal.
      sprite: {fileID: 21300000, guid: be3e007689ed1824e88c3dfb2f357443, type: 3}
      videoClip: {fileID: 0}
    popupShown: 0
  - pages:
    - title: Spell Crafting - Casting Point
      description: A Casting Point Rune determines the point in space where the Spell
        will initially appear. If not determined, the Spell will be directly cast
        from its Spellcaster's position.
      sprite: {fileID: 0}
      videoClip: {fileID: 0}
    popupShown: 0
  - pages:
    - title: Spell Crafting - Stats
      description: Above the Spell Tablet you can see you Spell's stats. Most Runes
        change the Spell's stats in some way.
      sprite: {fileID: 0}
      videoClip: {fileID: 0}
    - title: Spell Crafting - Stats
      description: Stat Runes have no innate effect on their own. They only apply
        specific stat changes to the Spell's stats. Stat Runes have blank Sockets
        and can be connected with other runes that also have blank Sockets.
      sprite: {fileID: 0}
      videoClip: {fileID: 0}
    popupShown: 0
  - pages:
    - title: Spell Crafting - Invoker
      description: Invoker Runes can be used to cast another Spell via the current
        Spell, depending on a defined Condition. You could make it so a Projectile
        invokes an Explosion once it hits something.
      sprite: {fileID: 0}
      videoClip: {fileID: 0}
    - title: Spell Crafting - Invoker
      description: 'To define the Condition and the invoked Spell, you must configure
        them in the Invoker Rune''s description. '
      sprite: {fileID: 0}
      videoClip: {fileID: 0}
    popupShown: 0
  - pages:
    - title: Money and Shopping
      description: When you defeat an enemy, every player gets some Money, which
        they can individually spend to get more Runes for their Spells.
      sprite: {fileID: 0}
      videoClip: {fileID: 0}
    - title: Money and Shopping
      description: The Rune Shop is where you can spend your Money for new Runes.
        It is located at the center of the Arena, indicated by the giant Obelisk.
      sprite: {fileID: 0}
      videoClip: {fileID: 0}
    - title: Money and Shopping
      description: In the Rune Shop, you get three options of Runes to purchase,
        each with their own price based on its Rarity. Also, you can spend some Money
        to Reroll your Rune options.
      sprite: {fileID: 0}
      videoClip: {fileID: 0}
    popupShown: 0
  - pages:
    - title: Main Objective
      description: In a real match, you will get together with other players (or
        not) to try to survive various enemy Hordes, using your Spells to defend
        yourselves.
      sprite: {fileID: 0}
      videoClip: {fileID: 0}
    - title: Main Objective
      description: Before each Horde, you will get some time to prepare your spells
        to your liking. Once the timer ends, the Horde starts automatically, but
        if you're ready before that, each player can press R to start the horde manually.
      sprite: {fileID: 0}
      videoClip: {fileID: 0}
    - title: Main Objective
      description: Once the Horde starts, enemies will start appearing and trying
        to attack you. They will keep appearing until the timer ends. When that happens,
        you must finish off every remaining enemy to end the Horde.
      sprite: {fileID: 0}
      videoClip: {fileID: 0}
    - title: Main Objective
      description: If your health reaches zero, you get downed, and will only get
        up once a Horde starts/ends. However, if every player is downed at the same
        time, you lose the game. To win, at least one player must be alive at the
        end of the final Horde.
      sprite: {fileID: 0}
      videoClip: {fileID: 0}
    - title: End of the Tutorial!
      description: You finished the Tutorial! You now understand the core mechanics
        of the game and are ready to try them in action. Also, if you want to keep
        experimenting with them without time and life pressure, you can go to the
        Training Arena.
      sprite: {fileID: 0}
      videoClip: {fileID: 0}
    popupShown: 0
